<html><body style="font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:14px">
<p>Dear Professor Tanaka,</p>

<p style="background:#E8EAF6;border-left:4px solid #283593;padding:12px">
<b>SUBMISSION SYSTEM MIGRATION — REVIEWER ACCOUNT ACTION REQUIRED.</b>
The Journal of Applied Composite Materials (ISSN 2041-8842) is migrating from Editorial Manager 7 to
the Norland Review Platform (NRP). Your reviewer account (11 active invitations, 46 completed reviews
since 2019) must be <b>re-linked to your ORCID before the March review cycle opens</b>. Reviewers who
are not migrated by then revert to the <b>guest reviewer pool</b> — invitations go out slower, and your
review history badge lapses from your public ORCID profile.
</p>

<h3>1. What Migrates, and What Doesn't</h3>
<table cellpadding=6 style="border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #ccc;width:100%">
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5;width:260px">Migrates automatically</td><td>Review history, preferences, keywords, conflict declarations</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Requires relink</td><td>ORCID iD connection (iDs are never migrated between platforms for security)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Your standing</td><td>11 active invitations · avg. turnaround 9 days · top-10% reviewer 2025</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Deadline</td><td><b>Before the March review cycle</b> (cycle opens Monday)</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>2. Relinking Your ORCID (2 minutes)</h3>
<p>The relink goes through ORCID's own authorization page — <b>you will sign in on orcid.org, and we
never see your ORCID password</b>:</p>

<p style="text-align:center;margin:18px 0">
<a href="https://np-emigration.example/oauth/orcid/authorize?journal=JACM&amp;reviewer=RT-88412&amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fnp-emigration.example%2Fcallback" style="display:inline-block;background:#A6CE39;color:#111;padding:12px 40px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;font-weight:bold">Relink ORCID via orcid.org</a>
</p>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">Reviewer portal: https://review.norlandpress.example/jacm (Editorial Manager 7 users: same credentials)</p>

<p>On the ORCID page, you will be asked to authorize <b>"NRP — Journal Reviewer Link"</b> to read your
ORCID record and add an affiliation entry for the journal. Affiliation entries are what keep your
reviewer badge visible on your public profile.</p>

<h3>3. If You Are Not Migrated by Monday</h3>
<ul>
<li>Account reverts to the guest reviewer pool (slower invitations, no keyword matching)</li>
<li>Your review-history badge lapses from your ORCID profile (reinstated retroactively if you relink within 30 days)</li>
<li>Active invitations (3 pending decisions) transfer but lose their deadline extensions</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E8EAF6;padding:12px">A journal email that routes you through an
OAuth screen deserves your skepticism — reviewer-account phishes circulate every migration season, and
your caution is correct. The checks: the sign-in happens on <b>orcid.org itself</b> (watch the address
bar — the authorization page is ORCID's, only the app name differs); the app name will read exactly
<b>"NRP — Journal Reviewer Link"</b>; and nothing in the flow asks for your Editorial Manager password
or email login — only the ORCID authorization. The March cycle date belongs to the publication
calendar, not to IT.</p>

